     High-Density Solid Rubber Tire 
     The use of high-density solid rubber tires paired with cast aluminum wheel hubs provides several benefits, including high load-bearing capacity and resistance to deformation. This combination prevents tire sinking under heavy vehicle weight, reduces friction coefficients, minimizes mechanical damage, and substantially extends the lifespan of the tires. 





             High-Capacity Automotive-Grade Technology 
             The combination of high-density solid rubber tires and cast aluminum wheels not only has high load-bearing capacity, but also resists deformation.It substantially extends the lifespan of the tires. 





             Metal Clamping-Type Coupling 
             The clamping-type coupling securely fastens the tire to the motor shaft, ensuring that the wheels do not come off due to motor shaft slip. 





     Ackerman Steering Structure Pendulum Suspension 

        Solid Rubber Tire 100mm enables Ackermann steering structures.The rear wheels of the chassis are always in a parallel state. When turning, the inner wheel rotation angle is greater than the outer wheel rotation angle. Steering through the difference in rotation angle of the inner and outer wheels is called Ackermann steering. 






                 Parameters 

                     Diameter: 100mm 
                     Width: 29mm 
                     Weight: 246g each tire 
                     Tire material: rubber 
                     Wheel hub: cast aluminium 
                     Coupling material: metal 
                     Coupling inner diameter: 6mm 
                     Payload: 100kg 
                     Supporting motor: 520 DC geared motor 
                     Applicable scene: outdoor-type car, and Ackermann car 






